{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392655-on-player-characters-and-sorcery","id":1392655,"title":"On Player Characters and Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-29T13:21:00-07:00","id":1392655,"title":"On Player Characters and Sorcery","content":"Does anyone have any advice on how PCs can use Sorcery? Is it as simple as giving them access to a Purview for Marvels, or are there any ideas that are more in-depth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T13:36:34-07:00","id":1392658,"title":"","content":"A book for PC sorcerers is actually in the works, and it will have its own system for Magic... Currently though, there's not much you can do beyond what you suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:47:50-07:00","id":1392697,"title":"","content":"There is one way you can do without much problem: treat them as denizens, soy you can have a Hero level character without being properly a Scion.<br /> <br /> You have a calling related to being a sorcerer (or any name you prefer), one path related to your sorcerer origin and gain access to one purview and more from birthright (a Master sorcerer is an interesting option, using Guide).<br /> But you have only 1 purview and no PSP.<br /> Other than that I think it\u2019s basically the same rules as Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:33:12-07:00","id":1392704,"title":"","content":"I hope that callings like Witch, Mage, Priest, Shaman, and Wizard, are added to the game. Certain deities are built around these roles. Among the most famous, Odin and Amaterasu as divine shamans, Thorth as a divine Mage, Freya, the Morrigrue, and Isis as divine witches, Hestia as a divine Priest, and Mannan Mac Lir as divine Wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T17:41:19-07:00","id":1392706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392655-on-player-characters-and-sorcery?p=1392697#post1392697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one way you can do without much problem: treat them as denizens, soy you can have a Hero level character without being properly a Scion.<br /> <br /> You have a calling related to being a sorcerer (or any name you prefer), one path related to your sorcerer origin and gain access to one purview and more from birthright (a Master sorcerer is an interesting option, using Guide).<br /> But you have only 1 purview and no PSP.<br /> Other than that I think it\u2019s basically the same rules as Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let's remember that there are figures that used magic/sorcery to become gods. Apollonius of Tyana was once as famous as Christ, and more widely respected. There are legends of the goddess Isis, legends older than those of her being born a goddess, where Isis steals by sly trickery Ra's name. And by the power of Ra's true name made herself a goddess. <br /> <br /> There needs to be a path for sorcerers to climb to godhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T19:59:40-07:00","id":1392732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392655-on-player-characters-and-sorcery?p=1392706#post1392706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There needs to be a path for sorcerers to climb to godhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make a Magic User capable of reaching god levels, it\u2019s perfectly possible to treat him as a God, as it\u2019s possible to treat any character with Legend as a Hero. Maybe there is a difference between a Hero and Sorcerer, but in game terms they are very similar.<br /> <br /> In the end we need to watt for the official approach, but my solution is not totally bad...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T06:25:27-07:00","id":1392791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392655-on-player-characters-and-sorcery?p=1392704#post1392704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that callings like Witch, Mage, Priest, Shaman, and Wizard, are added to the game. Certain deities are built around these roles. Among the most famous, Odin and Amaterasu as divine shamans, Thorth as a divine Mage, Freya, the Morrigrue, and Isis as divine witches, Hestia as a divine Priest, and Mannan Mac Lir as divine Wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is that Sorcerers won't be divided up into Callings that way, partly because each of those categories comes with a value judgment that Scion's been trying to avoid so far. (Note, for example, the sidebar in Origin explaining why it uses &quot;sorcerer&quot; instead of &quot;witch.&quot;) Distinctions in methods of performing supernatural actions are already built into the game in the form of pantheon motifs, so it might be unnecessary in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T07:57:51-07:00","id":1392806,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, Sorcerers are divided by their traditions, which are all based off of real life traditions, like apparently one such tradition is the Benandanti an Italian tradition of people who use their caul to astrally project their soul to fight demons and witchs, Goetia and Chaos Magick are both making appearances I believe. Traditions seem to be the closest thing to like pantheon motifs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T08:24:36-07:00","id":1392812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392655-on-player-characters-and-sorcery?p=1392658#post1392658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A book for PC sorcerers is actually in the works, and it will have its own system for Magic... Currently though, there's not much you can do beyond what you suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have not heard this. Do you have a link that mentions this book? I only know of Mythos and Dragon right now beyond Demigod and God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T08:34:56-07:00","id":1392814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1392655-on-player-characters-and-sorcery?p=1392812#post1392812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have not heard this. Do you have a link that mentions this book? I only know of Mythos and Dragon right now beyond Demigod and God.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the book is called Saints And Monsters.<br /> <br /> It also will cover more options for Saints, as implied by the title","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"tha